---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import StarlightPage from "@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro";
import mark from "../assets/logo/tetsu-mark.svg";

const refusals = [
  {
    title: "No decorators",
    text: "A decorator cannot put an inferred type into a method's signature, so every handler would be annotated by hand — and the metadata it writes is a second program the compiler cannot read.",
  },
  {
    title: "No container",
    text: "Without runtime reflection, dependency injection is tokens and ceremony. One file that builds everything and hands it over is shorter, and a reader can follow it.",
  },
  {
    title: "No router of its own",
    text: "Bun already matches paths natively. A second matcher would be a second opinion on which route a request belongs to, and the two would one day disagree.",
  },
  {
    title: "No plugins",
    text: "A package is a hook, a controller or a function, used like your own code. Registration at runtime would make what runs for a route something to look up instead of something to read.",
  },
  {
    title: "No middleware chain",
    text: "Around next(), when a function runs is a property of the call stack. In a fixed slot it is a name, and the compiler can check the order.",
  },
  {
    title: "No dependencies",
    text: "The core depends on nothing. Validation is Standard Schema — an interface, not a package — so the schema library is yours.",
  },
];
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: "About",
    description: "Why Tetsu is called iron, what its oni with an iron club means, and the ideas the framework is built on.",
    template: "splash",
    hero: { title: "About" },
    pagefind: false,
    head: [
      { tag: "meta", attrs: { property: "og:title", content: "About Tetsu" } },
      { tag: "meta", attrs: { property: "og:type", content: "website" } },
    ],
  }}
>
  <div class="about not-content">
    <section class="opening">
      <Image
        src={mark}
        alt="The Tetsu mark: a red oni holding an iron club"
        class="mark"
        width={320}
        height={320}
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
      <div>
        <p class="kanji" lang="ja">鉄</p>
        <h1 id="_top">Tetsu means iron.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Not a metaphor for speed or elegance — the plain material. Iron does what it looks
          like it does: you can see where it is joined, and it holds. That is what the framework
          tries to be.
        </p>
        <p class="motto">No magic. Just iron.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>The oni and the iron club</h2>
      <div class="columns">
        <div>
          <p>
            An old Japanese saying goes <span lang="ja">鬼に金棒</span> — <em>oni ni kanabō</em>,
            “an iron club for the oni”. The oni is already the strongest creature in the story; give
            it an iron club and nothing stands in its way. It is said of someone capable who has just
            been handed the right tool.
          </p>
          <p>
            In the mark, the oni is the developer, who already knows the domain, the data and the
            users. Tetsu is the club: plain iron that adds weight to every blow and stays out of the
            way of the hand.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="details">
          <li><strong>Red</strong> is the colour of the <em>aka-oni</em>, the red oni of Japanese folklore.</li>
          <li><strong>The narrowed eyes</strong> watch. The compiler catches what would break before it runs.</li>
          <li><strong>No mouth.</strong> The framework does not talk: no hidden behaviour, no conventions to guess.</li>
          <li><strong>The club is iron, with rivets you can count.</strong> Every part is visible, and every joint is where you put it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What you write is what runs</h2>
      <p class="wide">
        Open any route and what happens to its request is written there: the path, the schemas, the
        hooks by slot, the handler. What a group or the whole application adds is written where the
        application is wired, and every instance is built there by hand. There is no
        registry, no file scanning and no reflection. What you read is the whole program.
      </p>
      <p class="wide">
        The types follow the same rule. A field is on the context exactly when it exists at that
        point of the request — the body after it was validated, the user after the hook that found
        them — and the compiler checks the order of hooks, what each needs and what each adds. A
        type that says something the program does not do is a bug, whichever side it is on.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What it will not do, and why</h2>
      <ul class="refusals">
        {
          refusals.map((refusal) => (
            <li>
              <h3>{refusal.title}</h3>
              <p>{refusal.text}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What it borrows</h2>
      <p class="wide">
        Tetsu is not a new paradigm. It recombines ideas that proved themselves elsewhere: a request
        lifecycle with named stages, as in Elysia, without the method chain; hooks in fixed places,
        as in Fastify, with their types inferred; controllers and explicit composition, as in Nest,
        without decorators or a container. The value is in the combination — and in holding each
        piece to the same rule. The <a href="/docs/more/comparison/">comparison</a> says what it
        costs and when another framework fits better.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block who">
      <h2>Open source</h2>
      <p class="wide">
        Tetsu is MIT-licensed and built in the open on GitHub. Questions, bugs and ideas go to the
        <a href="https://github.com/tetsujs/tetsu/issues">issue tracker</a>;
        anything else to <a href="mailto:hello@tetsujs.com">hello@tetsujs.com</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
        <a class="link" href="https://github.com/tetsujs/tetsu">GitHub →</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</StarlightPage>

<style is:global>
  :root:not([data-has-sidebar]) {
    --sl-content-width: 76rem;
  }
</style>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: 2rem 3rem;
  }
  .opening {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem 4rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .opening {
      grid-template-columns: 20rem 1fr;
    }
  }
  .mark {
    width: min(20rem, 70vw);
    height: auto;
    justify-self: center;
  }
  .kanji {
    font-size: 3rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--tetsu-red);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.75rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
    max-width: 38rem;
  }
  .motto {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .block {
    padding-block: 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }
  p {
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .wide {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .columns {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem 3rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
    }
  }
  .columns p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .details {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }
  .details li {
    padding-inline-start: 1rem;
    border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--tetsu-red);
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .details strong {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  .refusals {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem 2.5rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 50rem) {
    .refusals {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }
  .refusals h3 {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .refusals p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .button {
    padding: 0.7rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
    background: var(--tetsu-red);
    color: #fff;
  }
  .link {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
</style>
